# Which files EAS Build uploads. When this file exists, eas-cli uses it
# INSTEAD of .gitignore to build the archive.
#
# It has to exist because .gitignore excludes /mobile-app and
# /mobile-app-patient so they stay out of the Vercel web build. EAS archives
# from the repository root and then looks for the app at
# projectRootDirectory ("mobile-app"), so those rules stripped the whole app
# out of the upload and the builder failed with:
#   "package.json does not exist in /Users/expo/workingdir/build/mobile-app"
# mobile-app/assets and mobile-app/plugins are also untracked, so they would
# have gone missing even though app.json references both.
#
# Because .gitignore is bypassed, every secret has to be re-excluded here.
# Do not remove the .env rules.

# Secrets — never upload to a build worker
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.capture

# Dependencies and build output — EAS installs and builds these itself
node_modules/
.next/
.vercel/
.git/
dist/
build/

# Local tooling and scratch files
.devin/
.claude/
.windsurf/
.codeium/
*.log
build-log*.txt
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
